Hi Dalton,

Standard box plots are not CI (see for ex.: 
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Box_plot). Thus, I think it's not a good idea
to suppress these grey lines (representing the CI). If you still want to,
you could do the following:

1) Put the attached "newfunction.R" file in your working directory (where
you have your gof object). This file is a lightly modified version of the
plot.gofobject function.

2) Make sure that you have a functional working environment by plotting your
gof object.


3) Write the following code in you R console:
source("newfunction.R")
pdf("gof_plots_without_IC.pdf") #redirect output in a pdf
newfunc(<m.gof>,IC=FALSE) # replace <m.gof> with the names of your gof 
object
dev.off() # close the pdf


The pdf "gof_plots_without_IC.pdf" will not contain any IC...


Hope that helps,
Victorin



