Message-ID: <010C59DD-C990-420C-896D-15B7707A4F29@stat.psu.edu>

Hi Charles.  You're not doing anything wrong; it's simply that ergm  
(the package, which is one of the statnet packages) has changed.  It  
now produces slightly different output.
If you're nervous about this, it is possible to get exactly the same  
output by re-installing the version of ergm that was current at the  
time of the article, namely, ergm version 2.1 (see p. 9 of the  
article, where all the version numbers are listed).  All of the old  
versions are available on CRAN, though they are only in source code  
(not pre-compiled binary) form.

Best wishes,
Dave




