Hello, Philip.
I usually import *.csv this way: first import it as matrix, than convert
matrix object to network objetc.
data.mat<-as.matrix(read.table("DATA"))
datan.net<-as.network(data.mat)
as.network function has several arguments for loops, directed graphs, etc.
You can check it out by executing help(as.network).
Here is a reference to some R-related SNA resources:
http://jeromyanglim.blogspot.com/2009/08/social-network-analysis-resources-for-r.html
Best wishes,
Alexander.

