Hi Scott.  Your question (which actually turned out to be a bit  
tricky) prompted a bit of back-and-forth among the statnet developers,  
and Carter pointed out that you should be able to get around this  
error by adding the argument 'names.eval', as in

defense.net <- network(defense.csv, directed=F, loops=F, hyper=F,  
multiple=F, bipartite=F, ignore.eval=F, names.eval="edgevarname")

Here, "edgevarname" should be whatever you'd like that name to be.

Thanks, Carter.
Dave


