Dear Statnet List,

Just in case anyone was spending time on this (or thinking about it), I wanted to give a heads up that I figured out what the issue was.

My problem was that I forgot to include a constant parameter (specified in the x argument to lnam). Pretty obvious in retrospect, but this meant that the model was forced to attribute the non-zero mean of my y observations to network autocorrelation effects. When I pass a vector of ones as the x argument, the results look much more reasonable.

Best,
Magnus

Ps. If anyone has any thoughts on this issue even now, I'd be grateful to hear about them, on-list or off.

