Oops, by the time I got to question 2 I had forgotten this was a strictly bipartite network.  So that answers the question I was wondering, since reciprocating ties must all be cross-sex. In that case you did indeed provide enough information.

Defining an absdiffincome dyadic covariate seems like the right first step.  From there, though, I think you may just be able to skip the step with the deletion and transpose, and simply use the mutual term with a "by" argument directly.  You state the question of interest in terms of women reciprocating ties with men, but unless you have some form of longitudinal data (which I am assuming you don't from the way you described it), then really, you only know that a dyad has reciprocated or not.  And in that case the term should work as is.  If you do have longitudinal data, and can actually say whether the woman sent the tie to the man first, or the man sent the tie to the woman first, then that's a whole other story.

Steve






