Hello David,
I use the ergm package Version 2.4-2 with the network package 1.6. I have already constructed several ergms with smaller networks without problems, so I think I did the basic things right.
I use the following code:

library(ergm)

netz <- read.paj("ignore.net")

* The network is a 10 MByte pajek network from a regional social network, with ignore (negative) ties. I can not send it, out of data privacy reasons. It has 114.000 vertices and 90.000 directed ties (binary)
* As a simple basic test model I use

model <- ergm(netz ~ edges)

After this command I get the first error message I already posted.

If I copy and paste the code you posted at that time afterwards (or directly after the library(ergm) command), and then use the "model <- ergm(netz ~ edges)" command I get the other
 error.

Error in ergm.pl(Clist = Clist, Clist.miss = Clist.miss, m = m, theta.offset = theta.offset,? : 
? unused argument(s) (conddeg = conddeg, MCMCparams = MCMCparams, MHproposal = MHproposal)

I also tried a second network with more ties (230.000) and the same number of actors. I can calculate simple measure for both networks with the sna package, but I get the same error for the other network.

kind regards and thanks for the answer
Richard



